Track 3: The Cattle-Cars Vault the Sun
- Story & Context: Scene mythology dictates that during the final eviction of the Galleria underground freight siding, the band locked themselves inside a rusted livestock railcar and cranked every synthesizer filter to infinite feedback until the pressure blew out the atrium skylights in a shower of glittering tempered glass. Transit officers reported hearing drums moving faster than humanly possible, accompanied by five hundred teenagers chanting from the catwalks before vanishing into the drainage canal tunnels beneath the rails. The track closes with the legendary self-oscillating loop that played untouched for four days: "When the red lights turn to vapor, ride the switch to the end!"
